# Security Policy

## Security Overview

Security is an important part of the Codexeron ecosystem.

This document explains general security practices related to Codexeron API resources.

---

# API Security Principles

Codexeron focuses on:

- Secure communication
- Protected credentials
- Controlled access
- Responsible integrations

---

# API Credentials

When API access becomes available:

Users should:

- Keep API keys private.
- Never publish credentials.
- Avoid sharing authentication information.
- Rotate compromised credentials.

---

# Responsible Usage

API users should:

- Use integrations responsibly.
- Respect usage limitations.
- Protect user data.
- Avoid abusive requests.

---

# Reporting Security Issues

If you discover a security issue:

Please report it through official Codexeron security channels.

Include:

- Issue description
- Affected component
- Steps to reproduce
- Technical details when available

---

# Public Disclosure

Please do not publicly disclose security vulnerabilities before they are reviewed and resolved.

Responsible reporting helps protect the entire ecosystem.

---

# Current API Status

The Codexeron API is currently under development.

Security practices will be expanded as API services become available.

